# EmailJS — powers the contact form.
# Get these from https://dashboard.emailjs.com
#
# None of these carry the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, and they must not: the browser
# posts to /api/contact, and that route calls EmailJS server-side. Prefixing
# any of them would inline it into the client bundle and hand anyone the
# ability to spend the monthly send quota — which is exactly the problem the
# server route exists to solve, since EmailJS gates domain allowlisting behind
# a paid plan.
#
# In EmailJS → Account → Security, both of these must be ON:
#   · Allow EmailJS API for non-browser applications  (server-side sending)
#   · Use Private Key                                  (makes the key required)
#
# Set all four in Vercel (Project → Settings → Environment Variables) before
# deploying. Without them the form returns a 503 telling visitors to email
# directly, rather than failing silently.

EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
EMAILJS_PRIVATE_KEY=
